==========================================================================================
FINDING: can that regime split be computed on eval too?
==========================================================================================

WHAT EVAL CARRIES
  matchId blank on         69,171 of 69,171 rows (100.00%)
  targetAllocation blank on 69,171 of 69,171 rows — eval labels live in BenchRec_cash_v1.0_solution.csv
  A_allocation populated on 37,123 of 37,123 A rows, 22,779 distinct keys

  So group membership is NOT given for eval. In train the regime is computed over
  the A rows sharing a B row's matchId. The only route without matchId is to
  reconstruct that A set from the keys the label names: take every A row whose
  A_allocation is in the target set. Whether that is the same set is testable on
  train, where matchId gives the answer.

VALIDATING THE RECONSTRUCTION ON TRAIN (matchId is the ground truth there)
  multi-key B rows tested: 6,678
    reconstructed A set identical to the matchId group: 4,302 (64.42%)
    over-collected  (picked up A rows from other groups): 2,376 (35.58%)
    under-collected (missed A rows in the group):         0 (0.00%)

  A key is not private to one group — a target key can also sit on A rows that
  belong elsewhere, so the reconstruction only ever adds rows, never loses them.
  What matters is whether those extra rows change the answer.

  regime, matchId group -> reconstructed group:
       repeat -> repeat     5,544
      neither -> neither      940
    partition -> partition    142
    partition -> repeat        35   <-- changed
       repeat -> partition     11   <-- changed
      neither -> repeat         6   <-- changed
  regime unchanged: 6,626 of 6,678 (99.22%)

  fraction of A rows at B's exact amount — same rows, both groupings (%):
         matchId groups  reconstructed  error
    0.0           14.54          14.68   0.14
    0.1            0.04           1.50   1.46
    0.2            0.03           1.15   1.12
    0.3            0.24           0.57   0.33
    0.4            0.09           0.39   0.30
    0.5            5.12           5.00  -0.12
    0.6            0.64           0.87   0.23
    0.7            2.62           3.80   1.18
    0.8            2.50           9.01   6.51
    0.9            3.94          14.76  10.82
    1.0           70.23          48.26 -21.97
  largest bucket error: 21.97 points

  VERDICT
    regime split          — COMPUTABLE on eval; the reconstruction reproduces train's own answer for 99.22% of rows.
    fraction distribution — NOT COMPUTABLE on eval. The extra A rows dilute the
      fraction, moving the 1.0 bucket by 21.97 points on train.
      Reporting it for eval would be reporting an artefact of the reconstruction.
      What would be needed: matchId, or any per-row group identifier, in the eval
      file — or an A-side group column in the solution. Neither exists.

