    The first is what makes the label consistent within a group; the second is what
    grouping eval's B rows by target set actually needs, and it is the weaker of the
    two. 6.59% of target sets are shared across groups, so the
    B side of the example below is reconstructed on the same footing as the A side:
    mostly right, not guaranteed, and it may include rows from another group.

